 [17592186403034 1081 "$(-3,1)$ and $(3,5)$" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403034 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403034 1084 #uuid "3d165dca-76a6-5440-b19b-8c808cb523b0" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403035 1081 "$(1,3)$ and $(1,5)$" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403035 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403035 1084 #uuid "523960b9-215b-5ec5-9e2e-830b99e6b9c5" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403036 1068 #edb/ref 17592186403037 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403036 1069 "q-51432" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403036 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403036 1071 "![](images/0c/0c8969fae3e21c8e5f5019509636e2307211921d742e6f067d9ee1c50499541b.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the function $y=f(x),$ defined on $[-3,3].$ Find the intervals on which the function $f(x)$ is concave up." 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403036 1072 #uuid "b1beed24-efd2-587e-8b4f-b044374db684" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403036 1074 "The concavity of a function refers to the direction in which its graph curves.\n\n- If the graph curves upward, like a \"smile\" ($⌣$), then the graph is said to be *concave up*.\n\n- If the graph curves downward, like a \"frown\" ($⌢$), then the graph is said to be *concave down*.\n\nIt's helpful to remember the mnemonic \"concave down like a frown.\"\n\nWe can see that the function is curved upwards like a smile ($⌣$) over the intervals $(-3,-1)$ and $(1,3).$\n\n![](images/ae/ae9ce6ca2597a4d5d1ca150c1e97d7c7a0a35f59fe5d6421b75203c6882d2052.png)" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403037 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403038 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403037 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403039 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403037 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403040 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403037 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403041 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403037 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403042 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403037 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403037 1077 "selection" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403037 1079 #edb/ref 17592186403042 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403037 1080 #uuid "38c59fe2-2779-5ba6-9c0d-69d20ff0ea27" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403038 1081 "$(-3,0)$ only" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403038 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403038 1084 #uuid "0e973d9a-0f09-5900-bf22-eef66722e865" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403039 1081 "$(1,3)$ only" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403039 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403039 1084 #uuid "47cac611-9920-5c71-952f-dd8cb39ccdf9" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403040 1081 "$(-3,-1)$ only" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403040 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403040 1084 #uuid "4042983e-d1df-528a-8fe4-25f17290d359" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403041 1081 "$(-1,1)$ only" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403041 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403041 1084 #uuid "c7b0f23a-5c95-5614-8f48-1c8705ee4818" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403042 1081 "$(-3,-1)$ and $(1,3)$" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403042 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403042 1084 #uuid "f3e429b3-2ae0-5777-a461-216e6c6244c6" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403043 1068 #edb/ref 17592186403044 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403043 1069 "q-52413" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403043 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403043 1071 "![](images/75/75a7f3bfae55a97fbc0c05e2e0356d21de6ceabcc82ac3e1c965838a636f5ecc.png)\n\nWhich of the following systems of inequalities defines the shaded region shown above?" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403043 1072 #uuid "9187138f-ae2f-5a56-952a-6135b67724bf" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403043 1074 "Consider the line $y=3x+1.$ Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Also, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny\\ge 3x+1.\n$$\n\n    \n\nNow consider the line $y=2.$ Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Also, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny\\ge 2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines the shaded region is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y\\ge 3x+1 \\\\ y\\ge 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403044 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403045 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403044 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403046 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403044 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403047 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403044 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403048 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403044 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403049 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403044 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403044 1077 "selection" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403044 1079 #edb/ref 17592186403045 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403044 1080 #uuid "6391aa03-c66c-510d-8de3-714552c986fb" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403045 1081 "{\\begin{aligned}y\\ge 3x+1 \\\\ y\\ge 2\\end{aligned}" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403045 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403045 1084 #uuid "c6c66b28-305f-5672-966e-0edbadb3f68b" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403046 1081 "{\\begin{aligned}y\\ge 3x+1 \\\\ y\\le 2\\end{aligned}" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403046 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403046 1084 #uuid "22d57f63-0dab-54f1-a015-47cd4fa3ad27" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403047 1081 "{\\begin{aligned}y\\ge 3x+1 \\\\ y<2\\end{aligned}" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403047 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403047 1084 #uuid "c282cd0f-a1b4-575a-bd8d-6fbc31f00808" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403048 1081 "{\\begin{aligned}y\\le 3x+1 \\\\ y\\le 2\\end{aligned}" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403048 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403048 1084 #uuid "dcc09857-90e2-5fa6-8e10-a5896664af24" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403049 1081 "{\\begin{aligned}y\\le 3x+1 \\\\ y\\ge 2\\end{aligned}" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403049 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403049 1084 #uuid "076f9837-2705-5d0a-9c57-71c316b16391" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403050 1068 #edb/ref 17592186403051 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403050 1069 "q-52461" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403050 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403050 1071 "![](images/ba/ba01cf5268f2bd62835c925a5eb793c0d98663948899c9e9aba2eeacd37ff30a.png)\n\nWhich of the following systems of inequalities defines the shaded region shown above?" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403050 1072 #uuid "d48a81ca-ca4e-5354-bd11-f73315ba7d7f" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403050 1074 "Consider the line $y=2x+6.$ Since the line is dashed, the inequality is strict. Also, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny<2x+6.\n$$\n\n    \n\nNow consider the line $y=5.$ Since the line is dashed, the inequality is strict. Also, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny<5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines the shaded region is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y<2x+6 \\\\ y<5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403051 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403052 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403051 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403053 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403051 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403054 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403051 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403055 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403051 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403056 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403051 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403051 1077 "selection" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403051 1079 #edb/ref 17592186403053 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403051 1080 #uuid "057029ec-da64-5909-af01-3dd51581c107" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403052 1081 "{\\begin{aligned}y<2x+6 \\\\ y>5\\end{aligned}" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403052 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403052 1084 #uuid "599f73e4-3ca9-5922-b9a5-51c11d904876" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403053 1081 "{\\begin{aligned}y<2x+6 \\\\ y<5\\end{aligned}" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403053 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403053 1084 #uuid "88ca59a7-54b0-51b6-8e85-e1665efeaa4a" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403054 1081 "{\\begin{aligned}y\\le 2x+6 \\\\ y\\le 5\\end{aligned}" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403054 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403054 1084 #uuid "cc2ec7bb-7f05-5512-a12e-01138a6573c3" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403055 1081 "{\\begin{aligned}y>2x+6 \\\\ y<5\\end{aligned}" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403055 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403055 1084 #uuid "17af44de-3d26-5293-8028-23cd473e2e0b" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403056 1081 "{\\begin{aligned}y>2x+6 \\\\ y>5\\end{aligned}" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403056 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403056 1084 #uuid "b7ebc338-a51c-54a2-9008-89b303d45e94" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403057 1068 #edb/ref 17592186403058 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403057 1069 "q-54202" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403057 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403057 1071 "What is the center and radius of the circle with the equation ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=169?$" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403057 1072 #uuid "13dc47a1-270d-56c2-8deb-b105337fbddb" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403057 1074 "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the origin is \n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nSo, the equation ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=169$ represents a circle that is centered at the origin, with radius\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{2} & =169 \\\\ r & =\\sqrt{169} \\\\ r & =13.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we disregarded the negative solution for the radius since the radius of a circle must be positive.\n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(0,0)$ and its radius is $13.$" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403058 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403059 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403058 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403060 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403058 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403061 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403058 1075 