eration is positive. In a speed-time graph, the acceleration is given by the slope of the line. So, we need to find the times for which the slope is positive.\n\nWe see from the graph that the slope is positive from $t=0\\,\\text{s}$ to $t=30\\,\\text{s}.$ Therefore, the object is accelerating in this time interval." 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403072 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403073 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403072 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403074 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403072 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403075 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403072 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403076 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403072 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403077 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403072 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403072 1077 "selection" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403072 1079 #edb/ref 17592186403077 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403072 1080 #uuid "f193901b-aa88-5598-b883-d5711c39904d" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403073 1081 "From $70\\,\\text{s}$ to $80\\,\\text{s}$" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403073 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403073 1084 #uuid "1719b7cb-bb0a-512e-b4d0-2db46619b09d" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403074 1081 "From $30\\,\\text{s}$ to $80\\,\\text{s}$" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403074 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403074 1084 #uuid "538466f6-26ea-5ceb-93d4-bf50e00e92bf" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403075 1081 "From $30\\,\\text{s}$ to $70\\,\\text{s}$" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403075 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403075 1084 #uuid "0140ed8a-92fd-5826-aecd-2f790dfa3107" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403076 1081 "From $0\\,\\text{s}$ to $70\\,\\text{s}$" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403076 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403076 1084 #uuid "dfc348c6-96de-5702-89fd-0eab3b40e299" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403077 1081 "From $0\\,\\text{s}$ to $30\\,\\text{s}$" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403077 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403077 1084 #uuid "3b6efc88-a3cc-5c91-8eab-852285448c53" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403078 1068 #edb/ref 17592186403079 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403078 1069 "q-60145" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403078 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403078 1071 "The equation $-20{x}^{2}+60x-41=0$ can be written in the form $20(x+p)^{2}=q.$ Find $q,$ and solve the equation." 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403078 1072 #uuid "a1ac9dcc-ee5b-5438-8680-0a3c7af8b759" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403078 1074 "First, we multiply the equation by $-1$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-1)\\cdot (-20{x}^{2}+60x-41) & =(-1)\\cdot 0 \\\\ 20{x}^{2}-60x+41 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we move the constant term to the right-hand side, factor the coefficient of the quadratic term, and complete the square on the left-hand side.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}20{x}^{2}-60x+41 & =0 \\\\ 20{x}^{2}-60x & =-41 \\\\ 20({x}^{2}-3x) & =-41 \\\\ 20[{x}^{2}-2\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}x+{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}-{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}] & =-41 \\\\ 20[{(x-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}-\\frac{9}{4}] & =-41\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we expand the brackets, and write the equation in the required form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}20{(x-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}-20\\cdot \\frac{9}{4} & =-41 \\\\ 20{(x-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}-45 & =-41 \\\\ 20{(x-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2} & =45-41 \\\\ 20{(x-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2} & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $q=4.$ We now solve the equation using the square root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}20{(x-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2} & =4 \\\\ {(x-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2} & =\\frac{4}{20} \\\\ {(x-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{5} \\\\ \\sqrt{{(x-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{5}} \\\\ |x-\\frac{3}{2}| & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{5}} \\\\ x-\\frac{3}{2} & =\\pm \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ x-\\frac{3}{2} & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5} \\\\ x & =\\frac{3}{2}\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403079 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403080 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403079 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403081 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403079 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403082 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403079 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403083 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403079 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403084 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403079 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403079 1077 "selection" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403079 1079 #edb/ref 17592186403082 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403079 1080 #uuid "838eec31-f001-5f3e-95ff-aee58026f6f2" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403080 1081 "q=4,\\,x=2\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403080 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403080 1084 #uuid "5408298f-7273-5f8e-b08d-eb9052a72e9e" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403081 1081 "q=4,\\,x=\\frac{3}{4}\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403081 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403081 1084 #uuid "55c297c3-ce19-541b-8f15-0e1cff269acc" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403082 1081 "q=4,\\,x=\\frac{3}{2}\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403082 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403082 1084 #uuid "18ad6631-816d-504b-86a5-d5fe74a70d5e" 13194139533491 17592186045585 