b/ref 17592186045487 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403229 1071 "Which of the following equations has no solutions for $0\\le x<2\\pi ?$\n\nI. $4\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+1=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x$\nII. $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+10=2\\operatorname{csc}⁡x$\nIII. $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=2\\operatorname{csc}⁡x-6$" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403229 1072 #uuid "28fa7313-ebe9-5114-aa43-a48667cbf78a" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403229 1074 "We first simplify the given equations, and get\n\n- $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=-\\frac{1}{3}$\n- $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=10$\n- $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=6$\n\nNow, recall that the range of $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi $ is given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\in (-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [1,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nSo, the equation $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=k$ has no solutions for $k\\in (-1,1).$ \n\nTherefore, of the given equations, only equation I has no solutions." 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403230 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403231 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403230 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403232 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403230 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403233 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403230 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403234 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403230 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403235 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403230 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403230 1077 "selection" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403230 1079 #edb/ref 17592186403233 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403230 1080 #uuid "8ca79eb9-6a7d-56ad-a7b2-6517a75087f4" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403231 1081 "II and III only" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403231 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403231 1084 #uuid "36f640cb-1d0e-55cf-82bf-2bc2df4f2cbd" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403232 1081 "I and III only" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403232 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403232 1084 #uuid "2f4fdfad-f0bb-539a-b3dd-5135ecf4149a" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403233 1081 "I only" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403233 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403233 1084 #uuid "de09ab34-6244-5de9-adc0-7d2808c13ffa" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403234 1081 "III only" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403234 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403234 1084 #uuid "a347e69f-18e6-5a4a-896e-70ebdae9cbe6" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403235 1081 "II only" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403235 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403235 1084 #uuid "87a5d244-0e82-5176-9600-2dd50bb45515" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403236 1068 #edb/ref 17592186403237 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403236 1069 "q-66435" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403236 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403236 1071 "The equation ${x}^{2}+16x+164=0$ can be written in the form $(x+p)^{2}=q.$ Find $p+q,$ and solve the equation." 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403236 1072 #uuid "f70143e0-3f9c-51d2-946d-0c2579968816" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403236 1074 "We first move the constant to the right-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+16x+164 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+16x & =-164\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we complete the square on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+16x & =-164 \\\\ {x}^{2}+2\\cdot 8x+{8}^{2}-{8}^{2} & =-164 \\\\ (x+8)^{2}-64 & =-164 \\\\ (x+8)^{2} & =-100\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p=8,\\,q=-100,$ and $p+q=-92.$\n\nWe now solve the equation using the square root method.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+8)^{2} & =-100 \\\\ x+8 & =\\pm \\sqrt{-100} \\\\ x+8 & =\\pm 10\\,\\text{i} \\\\ x & =-8\\pm 10\\,\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has two solutions, $x=-8+10\\,\\text{i}$ and $x=-8-10\\,\\text{i}.$" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403237 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403238 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403237 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403239 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403237 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403240 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403237 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403241 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403237 1075 #edb/ref 17592186403242 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403237 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403237 1077 "selection" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403237 1079 #edb/ref 17592186403240 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403237 1080 #uuid "042ad804-2249-5399-b919-45947b7e0d31" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403238 1081 "p+q=-108,\\,x=10\\pm 8\\,\\text{i}" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403238 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403238 1084 #uuid "8b7d8b31-ae04-5df6-aeb1-961f777e33b7" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403239 1081 "p+q=-108,\\,x=-8\\pm 10\\,\\text{i}" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403239 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403239 1084 #uuid "3477ce1f-9124-5c8e-aee7-0c19aaa37d5c" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403240 1081 "p+q=-92,\\,x=-8\\pm 10\\,\\text{i}" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403240 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403240 1084 #uuid "516e48e9-f368-58d1-b1c7-a413f32276d7" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403241 1081 "p+q=-92,\\,x=10\\pm 8\\,\\text{i}" 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186403241 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533491 17592186045585 true] [17592186